{"id":"mahabharata-3-150","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":150,"title":"पञ्चाशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 150 · Hanuman's blessing","summary":{"en":"Hanuman resumes his small form, embraces Bhima, and promises that in battle he will sit on Arjuna's banner and roar to strike terror into the enemy. He vanishes, and Bhima goes on towards the lotus pool.","kn":"ಹನುಮಂತನು ಸಣ್ಣ ರೂಪಕ್ಕೆ ಮರಳಿ ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ಅಪ್ಪಿಕೊಂಡು, ಯುದ್ಧದಲ್ಲಿ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಧ್ವಜದಲ್ಲಿ ಕುಳಿತು ಶತ್ರುಗಳಿಗೆ ಭಯ ಹುಟ್ಟಿಸುವಂತೆ ಗರ್ಜಿಸುವೆನೆಂದು ವಾಗ್ದಾನ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅವನು ಮಾಯವಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಭೀಮನು ಕಮಲಸರೋವರದತ್ತ ಸಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"हनुमान फिर छोटा रूप धरकर भीम को गले लगाते हैं और वचन देते हैं कि युद्ध में वे अर्जुन की ध्वजा पर बैठकर गर्जना करेंगे जिससे शत्रु भयभीत होंगे। वे अन्तर्धान हो जाते हैं, और भीम कमल-सरोवर की ओर बढ़ते हैं।","te":"హనుమంతుడు చిన్న రూపానికి వచ్చి భీముని కౌగిలించుకొని, యుద్ధంలో అర్జునుని ధ్వజంపై కూర్చొని శత్రువులకు భయం కలిగేలా గర్జిస్తానని వాగ్దానం చేస్తాడు. అతడు అదృశ్యమవుతాడు, భీముడు పద్మసరస్సు వైపు సాగుతాడు.","ta":"ஹனுமான் சிறிய உருவத்துக்குத் திரும்பிப் பீமனைத் தழுவி, போரில் அர்ஜுனனின் கொடியில் அமர்ந்து பகைவரை அச்சுறுத்தும்படி முழங்குவதாக வாக்களிக்கிறார். அவர் மறைய, பீமன் தாமரைக் குளத்தை நோக்கிச் செல்கிறான்.","ml":"ഹനുമാൻ ചെറിയ രൂപം വീണ്ടെടുത്ത് ഭീമനെ ആലിംഗനം ചെയ്യുന്നു; യുദ്ധത്തിൽ താൻ അർജുനന്റെ കൊടിയിൽ ഇരുന്ന് ശത്രുക്കളെ ഭയപ്പെടുത്തുന്ന ഗർജനം മുഴക്കുമെന്ന് വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു. അദ്ദേഹം മറയുന്നു; ഭീമൻ താമരക്കുളത്തിലേക്ക് യാത്ര തുടരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.150; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः संहृत्य विपुलं तद्वपुः कामवर्धितम् ।\nभीमसेनं पुनर्दोर्भ्यां पर्यष्वजत वानरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the monkey drew in that vast body, enlarged at his will, and embraced Bhimasena again with his arms."}},{"n":2,"text":"परिष्वक्तस्य तस्याशु भ्रात्रा भीमस्य भारत ।\nश्रमो नाशमुपागच्छत्सर्वं चासीत्प्रदक्षिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Embraced by his brother, Bhima's weariness vanished at once, and everything around him became favourable."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः पुनरथोवाच पर्यश्रुनयनो हरिः ।\nभीममाभाष्य सौहार्दाद्बाष्पगद्गदया गिरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the monkey, eyes brimming with tears, spoke again to Bhima out of love, in a voice choked with weeping."}},{"n":4,"text":"गच्छ वीर स्वमावासं स्मर्तव्योऽस्मि कथान्तरे ।\nइहस्थश्च कुरुश्रेष्ठ न निवेद्योऽस्मि कस्यचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Go to your dwelling, hero. Remember me in your talk, and while you are here, best of the Kurus, tell no one about me.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"धनदस्यालयाच्चापि विसृष्टानां महाबल ।\nदेशकाल इहायातुं देवगन्धर्वयोषिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Mighty one, this is also the place and time when the divine and Gandharva women, sent out from Kubera's abode, come here.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"ममापि सफलं चक्षुः स्मारितश्चास्मि राघवम् ।\nमानुषं गात्रसंस्पर्शं गत्वा भीम त्वया सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My eyes too are fulfilled, for you made me remember Raghava, and I have touched a human body by being with you, Bhima.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"तदस्मद्दर्शनं वीर कौन्तेयामोघमस्तु ते ।\nभ्रातृत्वं त्वं पुरस्कृत्य वरं वरय भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So let seeing me not be in vain for you, son of Kunti. Honouring our brotherhood, choose a boon, Bharata.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"यदि तावन्मया क्षुद्रा गत्वा वारणसाह्वयम् ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रा निहन्तव्या यावदेतत्करोम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If I should go to Hastinapura and kill those petty sons of Dhritarashtra, I will do it right now, if you wish.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"शिलया नगरं वा तन्मर्दितव्यं मया यदि ।\nयावदद्य करोम्येतत्कामं तव महाबल ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Or if I am to crush that city with a rock, I will do your wish right now, mighty one.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु तद्वाक्यं श्रुत्वा तस्य महात्मनः ।\nप्रत्युवाच हनूमन्तं प्रहृष्टेनान्तरात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the words of that great soul, Bhimasena answered Hanuman with a delighted heart."}},{"n":11,"text":"कृतमेव त्वया सर्वं मम वानरपुंगव ।\nस्वस्ति तेऽस्तु महाबाहो क्षामये त्वां प्रसीद मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Everything has already been done for me by you, bull of monkeys. May you prosper, mighty-armed one; I ask your pardon, be gracious to me.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"सनाथाः पाण्डवाः सर्वे त्वया नाथेन वीर्यवन् ।\nतवैव तेजसा सर्वान्विजेष्यामो वयं रिपून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With you as protector, valiant one, all the Pandavas have a protector. By your very power we shall conquer all our enemies.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु हनुमान्भीमसेनमभाषत ।\nभ्रातृत्वात्सौहृदाच्चापि करिष्यामि तव प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told this, Hanuman said to Bhimasena: \"Out of brotherhood and affection I will do what pleases you.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"चमूं विगाह्य शत्रूणां शरशक्तिसमाकुलाम् ।\nयदा सिंहरवं वीर करिष्यसि महाबल ।\nतदाहं बृंहयिष्यामि स्वरवेण रवं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When you plunge into the enemy host, bristling with arrows and spears, and give your lion's roar, mighty hero, I will swell your cry with my own voice.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"विजयस्य ध्वजस्थश्च नादान्मोक्ष्यामि दारुणान् ।\nशत्रूणां ते प्राणहरानित्युक्त्वान्तरधीयत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And I will sit on the banner of Vijaya and send out dreadful cries that take your enemies' lives.\" Saying this, he vanished."}},{"n":16,"text":"गते तस्मिन्हरिवरे भीमोऽपि बलिनां वरः ।\nतेन मार्गेण विपुलं व्यचरद्गन्धमादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that best of monkeys had gone, Bhima, best of the strong, roamed the vast Gandhamadana by that same road."}},{"n":17,"text":"अनुस्मरन्वपुस्तस्य श्रियं चाप्रतिमां भुवि ।\nमाहात्म्यमनुभावं च स्मरन्दाशरथेर्ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Remembering Hanuman's body and his peerless splendour on earth, and recalling the greatness and power of Dasharatha's son, he went on."}},{"n":18,"text":"स तानि रमणीयानि वनान्युपवनानि च ।\nविलोडयामास तदा सौगन्धिकवनेप्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he searched through those lovely woods and groves, wanting the saugandhika forest."}},{"n":19,"text":"फुल्लपद्मविचित्राणि पुष्पितानि वनानि च ।\nमत्तवारणयूथानि पङ्कक्लिन्नानि भारत ।\nवर्षतामिव मेघानां वृन्दानि ददृशे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw forests bright with blooming lotuses and flowering trees, and herds of rutting elephants muddy from the mire, like banks of rain-giving clouds, Bharata."}},{"n":20,"text":"हरिणैश्चञ्चलापाङ्गैर्हरिणीसहितैर्वने ।\nसशष्पकवलैः श्रीमान्पथि दृष्टो द्रुतं ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The glorious one went quickly along the way, seen by deer with flickering glances, who with their does grazed on grass."}},{"n":21,"text":"महिषैश्च वराहैश्च शार्दूलैश्च निषेवितम् ।\nव्यपेतभीर्गिरिं शौर्याद्भीमसेनो व्यगाहत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Out of heroism, Bhimasena, fearless, entered the mountain frequented by buffaloes, boars and tigers."}},{"n":22,"text":"कुसुमानतशाखैश्च ताम्रपल्लवकोमलैः ।\nयाच्यमान इवारण्ये द्रुमैर्मारुतकम्पितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trees with branches bent by flowers and soft, copper-coloured sprouts, shaken by the wind, seemed to be begging him in the forest."}},{"n":23,"text":"कृतपद्माञ्जलिपुटा मत्तषट्पदसेविताः ।\nप्रियतीर्थवना मार्गे पद्मिनीः समतिक्रमन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the way he passed lotus ponds, with their lotuses folded like hands, visited by drunken bees, with banks and groves lovely to see."}},{"n":24,"text":"सज्जमानमनोदृष्टिः फुल्लेषु गिरिसानुषु ।\nद्रौपदीवाक्यपाथेयो भीमः शीघ्रतरं ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"His mind and eyes held by the blossoming mountain slopes, with Draupadi's words as his provision, Bhima went faster still."}},{"n":25,"text":"परिवृत्तेऽहनि ततः प्रकीर्णहरिणे वने ।\nकाञ्चनैर्विमलैः पद्मैर्ददर्श विपुलां नदीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the day was turning, in a forest scattered with deer, he saw a broad river with clear golden lotuses."}},{"n":26,"text":"मत्तकारण्डवयुतां चक्रवाकोपशोभिताम् ।\nरचितामिव तस्याद्रेर्मालां विमलपङ्कजाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was full of excited karandava ducks, adorned with chakravaka birds, like a garland of spotless lotuses made for that mountain."}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्यां नद्यां महासत्त्वः सौगन्धिकवनं महत् ।\nअपश्यत्प्रीतिजननं बालार्कसदृशद्युति ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that river the mighty one saw a great saugandhika forest, a joy to see, bright as the morning sun."}},{"n":28,"text":"तद्दृष्ट्वा लब्धकामः स मनसा पाण्डुनन्दनः ।\nवनवासपरिक्लिष्टां जगाम मनसा प्रियाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing it, the son of Pandu got what he wanted, and in his mind went to his beloved, worn out by life in the forest."}}]}]}